ed 48) as the catalog files them - Horsemanship is a Pilot skill in this book and its own catalog category, so it is offered by name; the catalog''s Cowboy category has no Nightbane skill and is left out. The magical understanding of all languages is the ''Language: All (magical)'' row at the 89% printed (read on a render). Prowl 40% and swim 50% print no per-level figure. EQUIPMENT: ''Hollow Men who act as NSB agents get the full agent kit, including walkie-talkies, handguns and sub-machineguns'', plus full body armor (A.R. 16, 260 S.D.C.) and assault rifles (typically M-16s) against dangerous criminals. Resolved: walkie-talkie = Hand-Held Communicator (printed 225, ''basically an enhanced walkie-talkie''); handgun = the Model 951R Semi P Full Auto Beretta (printed 212), the nearest the chapter sells to the Beretta 95 machine pistol the NSB entries name on printed 166 and 201; sub-machinegun = a choice of the eight on printed 214-215 (the entry names none); armor = Hard Armor (printed 223), the chapter''s only A.R. 16 / 260 S.D.C. suit; assault rifle = 5.56mm M16 & M16A1 (printed 216). The kit is written for Hollow Men serving as NSB agents, which the entry says a large number are. MONEY: the entry prints none."
