# Namtar (Hollow Men)

## Lore

The Namtar are a race of tiny pseudo-insects from another dimension: repulsive beetle-like creatures with a slimy carapace and eight legs. Some scurry around the great palaces of the Nightlords, but more often they ride inside their constructs, the Hollow Men.

Like some insects the Namtar build with blood, mud and their own noxious secretions, and unlike any insect they use magic to give their creations a semblance of life. They build human-sized mannequins around themselves, like larvae in a cocoon, that walk, run, fight and pass for human. Hollow "Men" may be male or female, and can be made to look demonic or monstrous, but the Nightlords have ordered human-looking constructs to serve as their agents on Earth.

Thousands of Namtar-bearing Hollow Men now walk the streets, and many are members of the NSB, the National Security Bureau. In conservative black suits and dark glasses that hide their impassive eyes, they are known as the "Men In Black" (the MIB), and they concentrate on "terrorist activities" - which includes the work of journalists, clergy, researchers, dissidents, Nightbane, sorcerers, psychics and anyone else looking into the Nightlord-controlled governments, Nightbane, magic and the paranormal.

Less sadistic than other Nightlord minions, the Hollow Men still have no mercy or sympathy for humans; beneath the construct is a demonic insect totally alien to human experience. They take the most efficient and direct path to a goal: threats if threats will do, and torture, murder and random violence without raising an eyebrow if those are necessary.

## GM Notes

Average life span is 500 years. As NPCs they average level 1D4+3.

Alliances and allies: the Nightlords and their minions; occasionally other powerful and evil supernatural beings.

Weapons and equipment: Hollow Men who act as NSB agents get the full agent kit, including walkie-talkies, handguns and sub-machineguns. Against dangerous "criminals" they wear full body armor (A.R. 16, 260 S.D.C.) and carry assault rifles, typically M-16s.
